// Title: SCR File Write Event
// Sigma ID: c048f047-7e2a-4888-b302-55f509d4a91d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Christopher Peacock @securepeacock, SCYTHE @scythe_io
// Date: 2022-04-27 | Modified: 2023-08-23
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects the creation of screensaver files (.scr) outside of system folders. Attackers may
//   execute an application as an ".SCR" file using "rundll32.exe desk.cpl,InstallScreenSaver" for
//   example.
// False positives:
//   - The installation of new screen savers by third party software
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Libraries/Desk/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_new_scr_file.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith ".scr" and (not((FolderPath contains ":\\$WINDOWS.~BT\\NewOS\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\WinSxS\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\WUDownloadCache\\")))
